## Approach

Create `src/sidereal_time.rs` as a single-file module implementing all 4 GMST models (IAU 1976, IAU 2006, ERA/IERS 2010, long-term), the Equation of the Equinoxes with 33-term Fourier complementary terms, and a convenience wrapper that computes obliquity/nutation internally. Reuse `planetary_args_iau2000` from `nutation/mod.rs` by widening its visibility to `pub(crate)` — the complementary terms use identical fundamental arguments (verified against C source: same coefficients, same normalization).

All functions are pure (`&`-only, no mutable shared state). The public API takes eps/nut in **radians** (matching our internal convention), diverging from C's degree-based `swe_sidtime0` signature. The polynomial GMST computations follow the C unit flow exactly (sidereal seconds for IAU 1976/2006, degrees for ERA) to preserve bitwise-exact floating-point behavior; radians→degrees conversion happens only at the EoE boundary.

Alternative considered: extracting fundamental arguments into a shared `fundamental_args.rs` module. Rejected — functions are small (13 + 18 lines), only two consumers. Widening visibility is simpler.

